  "lineage": "Ceremonial song of the Gê-speaking Mebêngôkre (Kayapó) of southern Pará and northern Mato Grosso, whose great naming ceremonies, among them the Bemp and Tàkàk festivals that confer ceremonial 'beautiful names' on children, are carried by days and nights of collective singing and dancing in the village plaza. Men sing together as they dance, keeping time with gourd rattles. Ethnographers have recorded these ceremonies, and Mebêngôkre communities also record their own.",
